
Keymap can be loaded dynamically by $LK,"loadKBD",A="MN:loadKBD"$ function.
This function take the name of a $FG,2$.KBD$FG$ file (like $LK,"French.KBD",A="::/azTempleOS/Keyboard/Layouts/French.KBD"$) and load it
in memory.

$FG,2$French.KBD$FG$ was loaded by default in $LK,"StartOS",A="::/StartOS.HC.Z"$ file by Adam task.
If you want change it, you can replace the filename with another keymap file.
If you want disabled it, you can comment or delete the function call in
$LK,"StartOS",A="::/StartOS.HC.Z"$ file : $FG,5$loadKBD("French.KBD", NULL);$FG$ and reboot your system.

To disbale temporary the keymap, you can call the $LK,"freeCustomKbd",A="MN:freeCustomKbd"$ function.

$FG,4$-------------------------------$FG$

To make a keymap file, you $FG,4$$BK,1$MUST$BK,0$$FG$ follow instructions below :

Each line is a definition of caracters for one scancode.
All codes can be in hexadecimal or just in decimal.

$HL,1$
$FG,1$
0x10; 97;  65; .;  1;  // a
$FG$
$HL,0$
The first column it's for the scancode. $FG,1$0x10$FG$ was the scancode to the first
alphabetic key $FG,8$("a" to an azerty keyboard and "q" to an qwerty keyboard)$FG$

The second column is for "normal" key $FG,8$(without combo key)$FG$. It takes a position
code in the ASCII table. $FG,1$97$FG$ is the $FG,2$"a"$FG$ code.

The third column is for $FG,6$SHIFT$FG$ combo key. Like the second column, It takes a position
code in the ASCII table. $FG,1$65$FG$ is the $FG,2$"A"$FG$ code.

The fourth column is for $FG,6$ALT$FG$ combo key.
The $FG,1$.$FG$ is a link to the second column value. Actualy, the value of the second
column is $FG,1$97$FG$. So, the dot ($FG,1$.$FG$) take the 97 value. 
A dot can be used only from third column to the fifth column $FG,8$(because it's take
a value from the second column)$FG$.
$FG,6$ALT$FG$ combo is not supported natively by the kernel. You can make your own
ALT key combo in $LK,"HomeKeyPlugIns",A="::/HomeKeyPlugIns.HC.Z"$ and find function control to your keymap.

The fifth column is for $FG,6$CTRL$FG$ combo. You can find all CTRL combo in the
$LK,"KernelA",A="FL:::/Kernel/KernelA.HH,3441"$ but you can't use defined word in $FG,2$.KBD$FG$ file. You $BK,1$MUST$BK,0$ use values only.

Enjoy !

